  "topic": "Read and write Waw (و) at the beginning, middle and end of words, with Fatha, Kasra and Damma.",
  "minutes": 10,
  "learn": [
    {
      "en": "This is Waw. Like 'w' in 'water' or 'wave'. Lips round together — also sounds like 'oo' in 'moon'!",
      "title": "Meet Waw!",
      "ar": "و",
      "aud": "c-0-ar",
      "tr": "Waw"
    },
    {
      "en": "A small circular loop with a curved tail going down — like a hook or a lollipop! Waw looks like a WAVE or a HOOK — W for Water, W for Waw! It also means 'and' in Arabic!",
      "title": "How to write Waw"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a fatha, Waw says “wa”.",
      "title": "Waw with fatha",
      "ar": "وَ",
      "aud": "c-2-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a kasra, Waw says “we”.",
      "title": "Waw with kasra",
      "ar": "وِ",
      "aud": "c-3-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a damma, Waw says “wo”.",
      "title": "Waw with damma",
      "ar": "وُ",
      "aud": "c-4-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "“Ablution and prayer”",
      "title": "Sentence of the lesson",
      "ar": "وُضُوءٌ وَصَلَاةٌ",
      "aud": "c-5-ar",
      "tr": "Wudu'un Wa Salah"
    }
  ],
